    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3">

                <pb facs="0106" n="2" xml:id="pg2"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G/90: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay (Wright) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-04-01T16:00:00-03:30">April 1, 1932—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. I infer that Uruguay’s attitude at meeting of the Board of Pan American Union
                    April 5th will be that of no opposition to postponement of Conference for a
                    definite period of from 6 months to 2 years if proposed by Brazil or any other
                    country, but of objection to indefinite postponement as jeopardizing spirit of
                    Pan-Americanism and objects of conferences.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
